  "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
